---
description: Portfolio project rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Repo layout: Next.js 16 frontend at the root, Python FastAPI backend in /backend. The browser only calls /api/* on the Next origin; next.config.ts rewrites those to BACKEND_URL. Do not add API route handlers in src/app/api for chat, contact or github.
- Stack: Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind 3.4, Framer Motion. Before using an unfamiliar Next 16 API, check node_modules/next/dist/docs.
- All site copy lives in src/constants/index.ts. Components read from it. Never hard-code copy in components. The assistant's knowledge lives in backend/data/knowledge.json: keep both in sync when facts change.
- Never invent facts, metrics, dates, employers or links. If a fact is missing, leave a `TODO(jazib)` comment and tell me. Only show skills, projects and repos that are marked verified.
- Design tokens live in tailwind.config.ts and globals.css. No ad-hoc hex colors in components.
- Motion uses Framer Motion and must respect prefers-reduced-motion. Do not animate every element.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, visible focus rings, text contrast >= 4.5:1, tap targets >= 44px.
- Secrets only in backend/.env or .env.local, never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never committed.
- After each task run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` (frontend) or `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .` (backend), fix errors, then summarize in <= 5 bullets. Do not refactor unrelated files. Do not paste whole files into chat.
